-- =============================================================================
-- Hazard zone: the pine forest around St. Egyden am Steinfeld / Bahnhofsiedlung
--
-- Wildfires have occurred here, so the forest is monitored in full.
--
-- Source: OpenStreetMap forest polygons (landuse=forest / natural=wood) in the
-- area, unioned with PostGIS and split into connected components
-- (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). The union yields TWO bodies about
-- 253 m apart — separated by the rail/road corridor the Bahnhofsiedlung sits
-- on — so they are stored as two rows: the column type is GEOMETRY(Polygon),
-- one polygon per row. Together they cover roughly 26.6 km².
--
-- Outlines are simplified with ST_SimplifyPreserveTopology at a 0.0004°
-- tolerance (~45 m), which cuts 1037 positions to 270 while changing the
-- enclosed area by well under 1 %.
--
-- Re-runnable: ON CONFLICT updates in place, so applying it twice is a no-op
-- and it also re-activates a zone that was retired.
--
--   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml exec -T db \
--     psql -U openfirewatch -d openfirewatch < deploy/zones/st-egyden-foehrenwald.sql
-- =============================================================================

